                        "name": "14.C.1 Share of the voivodship in cargo traffic in seaports",
                      
                        "goal": "Goal 14. Life below water",
                      
                        "priority": "Strengthening the position of Polish sea ports, increasing the competitiveness of maritime transport and ensuring maritime safety",
                      
                        "definition": "Percentage share of the voivodeship in the total cargo turnover of seaports in Poland.",
                      
                        "unit": "percent",
                      
                        "dimensions": "total",
                      
                        "methodology": "Cargo turnover in seaports – the total amount of cargo moved through a port in a given period of time, either imported or exported by ships, when the transport is performed entirely or partially by sea; it includes international maritime traffic and domestic maritime traffic.Seaport – a commercial facility located at the interface between land and sea, appropriately equipped technically, technologically, and organizationally to handle trade carried out by sea, as well as to handle the sea and land transport means involved in their transportation.",
                      
